# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any PostgreSQL connection string — see DATABASE.md for provider guides
# (Neon, Prisma Postgres, RDS, Railway, local, zero-Docker local via
# `npm run db:local`, …). When your provider offers pooled and direct
# endpoints, use the DIRECT one — except Supabase, see below.
# Supabase: the "Transaction pooler" string for the running site, the
# "Session pooler" string (port 5432) for `npm run db:migrate`.
#
# When DATABASE_URL is not set, the variables the Supabase ↔ Vercel
# integration creates are read instead: POSTGRES_URL, POSTGRES_PRISMA_URL,
# POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING. Connecting the two projects is then enough.
#
# Prisma Postgres is paused: an address on db.prisma.io is skipped and the
# next variable is tried. PRISMA_POSTGRES=on uses it again.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECT_REF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# A remote host is connected to over TLS; a local one is not (DATABASE.md,
# "Configure the app"). Only for a remote Postgres WITHOUT TLS:
# DATABASE_SSL=false

# Verify the server certificate against this authority (Supabase: Database
# settings → SSL Configuration). Certificate text or a file path.
# DATABASE_CA_CERT=

# ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Authentication uses opaque, database-backed Prisma sessions. No auth secret
# is required; keep DATABASE_URL reachable so sessions can be created/read.

# ── Group video/audio calls ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Group calls use native peer-to-peer WebRTC. The browser connects peers
# directly; Postgres is used only to relay signaling (who is in the call and
# SDP/ICE messages). No third-party provider or API key is required — nothing
# to configure here.
#
# For calls to work across most networks, an ICE/TURN server is recommended
# for NAT traversal. STUN-only is used by default; you can add TURN by
# overriding ICE servers in src/components/Call/WebRTCRoom.tsx if needed.

# ── Media / object storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where uploaded photos and videos go. Postgres only stores the stable URL
# `/uploads/<uuid>.<ext>` — never a signed link.
#
# Supabase Storage (used first, when both are set). The Supabase ↔ Vercel
# integration sets these two for you. The key is the SECRET one
# (`sb_secret_…`, or the legacy `service_role` key) — never the anon /
# publishable key, and never a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=media
# Largest file the bucket takes. Supabase's free plan stops at 50 MB a file;
# raise this (and the bucket's own limit) on a paid plan.
# SUPABASE_STORAGE_MAX_BYTES=52428800
#
# Or any S3-compatible bucket (R2, MinIO, AWS S3, Prisma Object Store).
# Aliases accepted: PRISMA_BUCKET_NAME, PRISMA_BUCKET_ENDPOINT,
# PRISMA_BUCKET_ACCESS_KEY_ID, PRISMA_BUCKET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,
# PRISMA_BUCKET_REGION.
# S3_ENDPOINT=
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# S3_BUCKET=
# S3_REGION=auto
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
#
# With neither set, files go to public/uploads on disk (local development).
# STORAGE_DRIVER=supabase|s3|local picks one by name.

# ── Public site / SEO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical production origin. Do not use a Vercel preview hostname.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://hyper.co.ke

# Optional public privacy-request inbox. Publish only a monitored address.
# PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL=
